expert_calibration_2026-07-09: reworded verifier gates against expert re-review feedback
  (Omega Approved-Task QC Action List). Applied to gdpval_task_quality_v18.md AND the
  variants that carry copies (slim, eval_gates_only, final_qc); backup in specs.backup-*/.
  FALSE-POSITIVE fixes (expert disagreed w/ Auto-QC): (1) construct_validity + discriminative_power
  now check the GOLDEN before flagging a 0%/always-fails rubric — golden-passes => legit difficulty,
  not a broken verifier (task 111 v9); (2) construct_validity: requiring prompt-grounded facts in
  ANY format is completeness, not over-penalization/format-rigidity (task 116 v2/v8/v9);
  (3) clarity: soft quantifier ("substantially all") is fine when backed by an enumerated set /
  objective fallback (task 111 v8); (4) missing_critical: criterion covered across a COMBINATION
  of rubrics is not a gap (task 111 feasibility) — strengthened with an explicit "name the rubric
  that would fail a wrong solution" trace; (5) construct_validity: before flagging a rubric as
  OVER-STRICT / over-specified, check the golden — golden-passes => demanding not over-penalizing
  (the lever the experts used on task 116); (6) outcome_coverage: a missing side-effect / output-dir
  check is sev1 polish (accept_with_fixes), not a gating sev2 (Luiz ruling, task 53). ADDED
  hard-fails (expert agreed): extract_text can't verify live/formula/no-hardcoding claims (task 24
  v19/v20); advisory wording should/preferably/such-as + broad "materially unsolicited" side-effect
