trajectory_qc_v18.6_2026-07-17: added trajectory-reliant LLM QC checks (inspired by OpenAI
  "Separating signal from noise in coding evaluations" — investigator reads model TRAJECTORIES,
  not just scores). Existing eval gates read only verifier_assertion_summary (pass/fail digest);
  these read the actual agent trajectories + deliverables under evals/<model>/trial_*/.../agent/ +
  artifacts/output/. FIVE checks: (E) intermodel_trajectory_consistency [NEW, advisory] — reward
  ordering vs visible trajectory quality across models + convergent core-rubric failure; owns the
  CROSS-FAMILY + trajectory-grounded call eval_capability_inversion refuses. (B) prompt_underspecification
  [NEW, advisory] — a legit rubric requirement the PROMPT never conveyed (silent omission). (D)
  prompt_misleading [NEW, advisory] — prompt wording actively steers toward a penalised approach
  (must quote the steering span). (A) construct_validity + (C) discriminative_power [AMENDED] — now
  also read a sampled failed / passed trial's real deliverable (build_failed/passed_trial_deliverable_digest)
  as concrete over-strictness / leniency evidence. Clean 3-way locus split: E=verifier wrong,
  B=prompt silent, D=prompt misleads. New module gdpval_qc/v18_trajectory_digest.py (3 string
  callbacks mirroring v18_verifier_summary; DROPS observation.content bulk; ~30k digest); callbacks
  auto-registered in v18_loader; precondition task_has_full_trajectories; _FIELD_CHAR_LIMITS entries
  (intermodel 60k, deliverables 40k). Tools: tools/build_ablation_corpus.py (joins the k=10/6-model
  eval drop with the labeled calibration goldens via symlinked evals/), tools/ablation_diff.py,
  tools/consistency.py. VALIDATED on the 5 labeled calibration tasks (24/48/53/111/116) with the
  k=10/6-model trajectories: new advisory dims = 0 marginal verdict impact (do-no-harm, proven via
  compute_verdict); amended blocking A stable on its catches (task_48=2/2/2, task_53=3/3/3);
  cross-dim convergence (A+E+B all flag task_48) = real defect. B/D wording tightened (evidence bar:
  B needs a 4-point checklist, D must quote the steering span) — cut noise 8->4 swings, verdict flaps
  2->1 task; residual task_116 D flap is the documented judgment-boundary (route to human). FOLDED
  into ALL default QC specs (Luiz, 2026-07-17: "all default QC calls should use these"):
  gdpval_task_quality_v18.md (cmd `qc`, now 30 dims), gdpval_final_qc.md (== v18.6, 12 dims), and
  gdpval_slim_qc.md (cmd `redflags` default, 14 dims) all carry the 5 checks. The checks are
  self-gating: E/B/D applies_when task_has_full_trajectories (needs >=2 models with agent/trajectory.json)
  and A/C's deliverable digests return None without artifacts/output — so bundle-time `qc` (no
  trajectories yet) is unaffected; they only fire once a corpus has trajectories. NOT promoted to
  blocking (E/B/D stay advisory; their borderline swings would destabilise verdicts if they gated).
  Reference spec kept at specs/gdpval_task_quality_v18_6.md. NEXT: seed calibration/v18_6/ goldens
  (trajectories kept) from the stable catches; optionally add to eval_gates_only.
